"That explains the cool bowl. A dry plate or bowl has almost no water in it, so the waves pass right through. It also explains why ice heats slowly: in ice, the water molecules are locked in place and can hardly turn. And because the bouncing waves are strong in some places and weak in others, the oven has hot spots and cold spots. The turntable carries the food through both.": "bbcacee823ab",
